WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.490
In temples across India,
worshippers bring lamps,

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.800
flowers and songs.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.150
Most Hindus worship a personal
God, with love and devotion.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.830
But in love, there are always
two: the one who loves,

5
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.810
and the one who is loved.

6
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.510
Or are there?

7
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.880
So is the soul one with God, part of God,

8
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.420
or forever different from God?

9
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:27.070
In this mission, you'll meet
two great teachers of devotion:

10
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.160
Ramanuja and Madhva.

11
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.190
Then you'll set their answers side by
side with the other great schools of Hindu

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.210
thought.

13
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.520
Your mission: find out how these
teachers relate the soul to God,

14
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.440
and why it matters for devotion.
